{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/361682-exigent-speculation-so-called-dirty-bombs","id":361682,"title":"Exigent Speculation: So called \"Dirty Bombs\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-06T16:19:52-08:00","id":361682,"title":"Exigent Speculation: So called \"Dirty Bombs\"","content":"All we know about the Dirty Bomb Exigents is that they're black market Exalted created from multiple donor Spirits, and that this produces an &quot;Abberation of Terrible Power&quot;<br /> <br /> The question is, what sort of Aberration could be created this way? Are the so called Dirty Bombs always the result of Blackmarket Exaltations? For Example, if a Forest settlement is to be besieged by an army of Fair Folk, could the City God and Forest God both contribute power to the resulting Exalt?<br /> <br /> The Unofficial Name given to the Dirty Bombs also has interesting implications-a dirty bomb is a bomb wih a small yield explosion but that releases large amounts of radiation or biological weaponry into the environment around it, causing little damage in the long term but severe damage in the long term.<br /> <br /> I've got the mental image of a forbidden god of some chaotic or destructive perview stealing an exigency from a sword spirit after the spirit modified it, put just a touch of his own juice into it, tricked a dumbass mountain god or earth Elemental(If Elementals can do Exigents) into sacrificing his life to empower, doing the same with a minor fire god/elemental, before recruiting the ancient god of a mighty tree(Or a king of the forest) and a few minor sadistic sea/storm gods to provide some remaining oomph and the other missing elements, before tinkering the exact configuration of the power so that there would be no caste mark and the anima would be real elemental energy, like a dragon blooded, and then just plopping it into some semi random peasant from the realm, just to see what happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T16:30:12-08:00","id":361706,"title":"","content":"I believe the term dirty bomb was selected less for the short term/long term distinction of its damage and more for the connotation that it's an inferior but still dangerous version of a terrifyingly powerful thing, one far more accessible to a relatively minor bad guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T17:15:55-08:00","id":361761,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone can &quot;customize&quot; an exaltation the way you are suggesting. Even for the greatest of the gods it is a divine miracle and a holy mystery. Autochthon and the Incarne who designed them did not know the whole of what they wrought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T22:43:53-08:00","id":362145,"title":"","content":"Anima:Most of the juice powerering the Exigency came from spirits asociated with the elements and the Forbidden Deity has a chaotic and destructive purview. the idea of having a banner of destructive elemental energy isn't that unlikely, and &quot;Caste Mark yes/know) sounds like one of those things that a deity might be able to influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T00:10:22-08:00","id":362179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/361682-exigent-speculation-so-called-dirty-bombs?p=361706#post361706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the term dirty bomb was selected less for the short term/long term distinction of its damage and more for the connotation that it's an inferior but still dangerous version of a terrifyingly powerful thing, one far more accessible to a relatively minor bad guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In order to get the full bang out of the &quot;dirty bomb&quot; metaphor, it helps to look at it from the perspective of the Sidereals as though they were Homeland Security.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T03:12:47-08:00","id":362253,"title":"","content":"From what's been said so far, my model for dirty bomb Exigents is the Abomination from the movie of <i>The Incredible Hulk</i>. Two different power sources get rashly mixed together with no testing, transforming the recipient into something very powerful but also mad with power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T03:31:29-08:00","id":362260,"title":"","content":"Just a thought maybe after passing through the possession of so many gods, elementals, what have you the exigency loses some of its stability and causes se unpleasant effects. Maybe its an exalt with a penchant for causing large amounts of collateral damage or is simply driven increasingly bonkers by the power. Having such unstable properties could give it the &quot;dirty bomb&quot; label.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/659-dominostro","name":"Dominostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar659_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T07:09:43-08:00","id":362393,"title":"","content":"I feel like the expression of a dirty bomb Exigent is a thematic amalgam of its parts - which can be significantly powerful and horrific with particular combinations, at least accidentally.<br /> <br /> Like the Exigent of Plagues, Chosen of the Pale Lady, would look a particular way with disease-based and punishment-based powers. But cross-pollinate that with say the powers of a field god and the powers of a god of dead bodies and you have a potential Stratholme situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T15:44:45-08:00","id":362977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/361682-exigent-speculation-so-called-dirty-bombs?p=362393#post362393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the expression of a dirty bomb Exigent is a thematic amalgam of its parts - which can be significantly powerful and horrific with particular combinations, at least accidentally.<br /> <br /> Like the Exigent of Plagues, Chosen of the Pale Lady, would look a particular way with disease-based and punishment-based powers. But cross-pollinate that with say the powers of a field god and the powers of a god of dead bodies and you have a potential Stratholme situation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. I'm thinking an Exalt that's strange but relatively normal(Taking my given example, the Exalt might start by being really good with a sword with elemental powers that are primarily destructive in nature), but then as it grows more powerful, it's powers mix together in strange and interesting ways untill you get the aforementioned aberration of terrifying power<br /> <br /> They've mentioned that some Exigents will be able to switch from one type of charms(Abillity) to an other(essence) as their essence scores are raised, and that the exigent rules could be used to build an exalt with one or more &quot;apotheosis paths&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if Dirty Bombs aren't the reason for one or both of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}